# labwc autostart for the atlas kiosk.
#
# Install to ~/.config/labwc/autostart.
#
# IMPORTANT: labwc reads the FIRST autostart it finds — ~/.config/labwc/
# then /etc/xdg/labwc/ — it does not merge them. Dropping a bare kiosk line
# here would silently take away the taskbar, the desktop and the XDG
# autostart set, so the stock file is sourced first and everything the
# Raspberry Pi desktop normally starts still starts.

. /etc/xdg/labwc/autostart

# Screen blanking: nothing blanks the display unless an idle daemon is
# running, and none is on this host (checked: no swayidle, no
# xdg-screensaver). wlopm forces every output on at login in case one was
# left powered down, which is the state the board must never be found in.
# If blanking is later switched on in Raspberry Pi Configuration, it starts
# swayidle -- remove it again, or the board goes dark at 3am.
/usr/bin/wlopm --on '*' &

# lwrespawn is the Pi desktop's own restart helper: it is what keeps the
# panel alive, and it gives the kiosk the same treatment. Chromium dying at
# 4am must not leave a blank screen until morning.
/usr/bin/lwrespawn /opt/atlas/scripts/kiosk-start.sh &
